Question: Within how many hours must a transmission system operator re-energise the network after a blackout according to the network code on emergency and restoration?

Answer: The corpus does not say. It contains no text of the network code on emergency and restoration (Regulation (EU) 2017/2196), so no time limit for re-energising the network after a blackout can be given. Regulation 2017/2195 only refers to 2017/2196 in passing (market suspension and settlement rules), and Regulation 2019/943 mentions that code only in connection with regional coordination centres supporting the consistency assessment of defence and restoration plans. Neither sets a number of hours.

