Question: On what basis is the price of redispatching and countertrading resources determined?

Answer: Under Article 35(5) of Regulation 2015/1222, generation units and loads give TSOs their redispatching and countertrading prices before the resources are committed. Pricing is based either on (a) prices in the relevant electricity markets for the relevant time-frame, or (b) the cost of the resources, calculated transparently on the basis of incurred costs. Generation units and loads must also provide ex-ante all the information needed to calculate these costs (Article 35(6)). Separately, Regulation 2019/943 Article 13(7) sets minimum financial compensation for non-market-based redispatching, but this is compensation, not the pricing basis asked about.

