Question: Can a balancing service provider still update its balancing energy bid after gate closure?

Answer: Generally no for balancing energy bids. Article 2(27) defines the 'balancing energy gate closure time' as the point when submission or update of a balancing energy bid for a standard product on a common merit order list is no longer permitted. Article 18(7)(b) likewise refers to providers changing their balancing energy bids 'prior to' that gate closure time. Balancing capacity bids may be updated only before the procurement process gate closure time (Art. 16(3)). The passages do not give the rules for updating integrated scheduling process bids after their gate closure (Article 24(6) is only referenced).

