Question: What options exist for setting aside border transmission capacity for the exchange of reserves?

Answer: The passages describe only one option in detail: allocation of cross-zonal capacity based on an economic efficiency analysis (Art. 42). It applies to the exchange of balancing capacity or sharing of reserves where the contracting period is over one day and contracting is more than one week ahead. TSOs of a capacity calculation region may propose it. It is limited to 5% of the previous year's available energy-exchange capacity on the border, or 10% of the installed technical capacity of new interconnectors, and the limit may not apply to DC interconnectors. Art. 42(2) also mentions co-optimised or market-based allocation processes (Art. 38(3)), and Art. 35 mentions a methodology under Art. 33(6). The passages do not set out either, so the full list of options is not given.

