Answer: The passages do not list the parameters that define a harmonised (standard) balancing energy bid. That list would be in Article 26, which is not provided. Article 2 defines terms that describe a product's timing and delivery: preparation period, full activation time, deactivation period, delivery period, validity period, mode of activation (manual or automatic) and divisibility. On your example, 'full activation time' is the period from the activation request to full delivery of the product. Article 2 also defines a 'standard product' only as a harmonised balancing product defined by all TSOs, without specifying its parameters.

