Question: How must the resources redispatched to relieve congestion be selected, and what is the only additional charge allowed for exchanging balancing energy across borders?

Answer: Redispatched resources must be selected from generating facilities, energy storage or demand response using market-based mechanisms, and be financially compensated (Art. 13(2) of Regulation 2019/943); non-market-based redispatching is allowed only in the limited cases listed in Art. 13(3). For cross-zonal exchange of balancing energy (or operating the imbalance netting process), the pricing methodology must not apply any additional charges, except a charge to compensate losses, and only if that charge is also taken into account in other timeframes (Art. 30(3)(c) of Regulation 2017/2195).

