Question: Can a balancing service provider still update its balancing energy bid after gate closure?

Answer: No. Under Article 24(3), after the balancing energy gate closure time balancing service providers are no longer permitted to submit or update their balancing energy bids. After that time they must only report any unavailable volumes of balancing energy bids to the connecting TSO (and to the DSO, if required) without undue delay. A separate rule for integrated scheduling process bids under a central dispatching model allows changes after the integrated scheduling process gate closure time, but only under the connecting TSO's rules. That rule covers integrated scheduling bids, not balancing energy bids.

