Question: What criteria guide a TSO when choosing between possible grid-security countermeasures?

Answer: When selecting remedial actions, each TSO must (Article 21(2)): (a) activate the most effective and economically efficient actions; (b) activate them as close as possible to real time, considering expected activation time and urgency; (c) consider the risks of failure in applying available actions and their impact on operational security (failures or short-circuits from topology changes, outages from active/reactive power changes on generating modules or demand facilities, and equipment malfunction); and (d) prefer actions that make available the largest cross-zonal capacity for capacity allocation while satisfying all operational security limits. Article 23(1) requires preparation and activation in accordance with these criteria.

