Question: Which body facilitates the regional procurement of balancing capacity, and what may it do as a last resort when the available remedial actions cannot deliver the minimum capacity?

Answer: Regional coordination centres facilitate the regional procurement of balancing capacity (Article 37(1)(k)); Article 6(8) adds that procurement itself is performed by the TSO and may be facilitated regionally. As a last resort, where available remedial actions (not including load shedding) are insufficient to reach the linear trajectory or the minimum capacities while respecting operational security limits, regional coordination centres may set out coordinated actions reducing cross-zonal capacities accordingly (Article 16(3)).

