Question: Can a balancing service provider still update its balancing energy bid after gate closure?

Answer: No, for balancing energy bids for standard products. After the balancing energy gate closure time, balancing service providers are no longer permitted to submit or update their balancing energy bids (Article 24(3)); the gate closure time is defined as the point when submission or update of such a bid is no longer permitted. After that, they must only report unavailable volumes to the connecting TSO. For integrated scheduling process bids under central dispatching, after each integrated scheduling process gate closure time the bid may only be changed under the connecting TSO's rules in the terms and conditions for balancing service providers.

