Question: What criteria guide a TSO when choosing between possible grid-security countermeasures?

Answer: Under Article 21(2) of Regulation 2017/1485, a TSO selecting remedial actions must: (a) activate the most effective and economically efficient actions; (b) activate them as close as possible to real time, considering expected activation time and urgency; (c) consider the risks of failure in applying the available actions and their impact on operational security (topology-change failures or short-circuits, outages from active/reactive power changes on generating modules or demand facilities, equipment malfunction); and (d) prefer actions that make the largest cross-zonal capacity available for capacity allocation while satisfying all operational security limits. Article 23(1) says actions are prepared and activated according to these criteria.

