Question: What options exist for setting aside border transmission capacity for the exchange of reserves?

Answer: The passages set out three allocation processes for cross-zonal capacity used for the exchange of balancing capacity or sharing of reserves. (1) Co-optimised allocation (Art. 40): capacity is allocated to energy bids and balancing capacity/reserve-sharing bids in a single optimisation, for contracting periods of up to one day and contracting at most one day ahead. (2) Market-based allocation (Art. 41): for contracting periods of up to one day and contracting up to one week ahead, based on comparing actual and forecasted market values, and capped at 10% of available capacity (with exceptions). (3) Allocation based on economic efficiency analysis (Art. 42): for contracting periods over one day and contracting more than one week ahead, capped at 5% of available capacity (10% of installed capacity for new interconnectors).

