Question: What criteria guide a TSO when choosing between possible grid-security countermeasures?

Answer: Under Article 21(2) of Regulation 2017/1485, when selecting remedial actions a TSO must: (a) activate the most effective and economically efficient actions; (b) activate them as close as possible to real-time, considering expected activation time and urgency; (c) consider the risks of failure in applying them and their impact on operational security (topology-change failures or short-circuits, outages from active/reactive power changes on generating modules or demand facilities, equipment malfunction); and (d) prefer actions that make available the largest cross-zonal capacity for capacity allocation while satisfying all operational security limits. Article 23(1) says remedial actions are prepared and activated according to these criteria.

