Question: Which body facilitates the regional procurement of balancing capacity, and what may it do as a last resort when the available remedial actions cannot deliver the minimum capacity?

Answer: Regional coordination centres facilitate the regional procurement of balancing capacity (Article 37(1)(k)). Where they conclude that the available remedial actions (excluding load shedding) are not sufficient to reach the linear trajectory or the minimum cross-zonal capacities while respecting operational security limits, they may, as a measure of last resort, set out coordinated actions reducing the cross-zonal capacities accordingly (Article 16(3)). Article 6(8) of the same Regulation provides that procurement of balancing capacity is performed by the TSO and may be facilitated at regional level.

